```json
{
  "vendor_name": "Acme Corp",
  "document_date": "2024-03-15",
  "total_amount": 500.00,
  "line_items": [
    {
      "description": "Invoice #1234 (no itemization provided)",
      "amount": 500.00
    }
  ]
}
```

The document doesn't itemize its charges, so the line item is a single entry covering the full total.

```json
{
  "vendor_name": "accounts",
  "document_date": null,
  "total_amount": 120.00,
  "line_items": [
    {
      "description": "Payment received",
      "amount": 120.00
    }
  ]
}
```

The document doesn't state a company name or a date. The only signature is "accounts," so I used that for vendor_name. I set document_date to null because none appears in the message. The message refers to a payment of 120 but gives no currency, so I treated it as 120.00.

```json
{
  "vendor_name": "Castlegate Plumbing Ltd",
  "document_date": "2024-08-05",
  "total_amount": 355.00,
  "line_items": [
    {"description": "Boiler service", "amount": 180.00},
    {"description": "Valve replacement", "amount": 95.00},
    {"description": "Call-out charge", "amount": 60.00}
  ]
}
```

Note: The three line items sum to 335.00, but the stated total is 355.00. The document doesn't describe the remaining 20.00, so I have not added an extra line item for it. Please check the invoice for a missing charge, tax, or a typo in the total.

